title: "Finite Contact Theory v0.9: The Multi-Floor Worldweave — A Forcing Audit of the E_8-Hexacode Spine"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Douglas"
    given-names: "Seth"
    email: "apsiape@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4708-3252"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Apsiape/finite-contact-theory-public"
abstract: "A public release of Finite Contact Theory, a long-range finite reconstruction program, now spanning nine chapters on three lines. The quantum-facing and finite-epistemics axes grow the Bell/CHSH boundary, rational Born weights, a native carrier grammar, an exact preparation gap, the identifiability and debt calculus, the inquiry calculus, four theorems on time, and a measured generative floor. The contact-interface line derives, by exact finite checks, a quaternionic state/receiver cell whose closure is the 24-cell and F_4 and whose measurement calculus forces the Born frame rule exactly where a triality Kochen-Specker obstruction forbids a global pointing (Chapter 8). This v0.9 chapter extends that line across cells: independently generated cells do not combine by tensor product but settle their D_4 triality boundary debts into a self-dual bridge code. The unique debt-free two-cell closure is the E_8 root system; local fusion is octonionic (nonassociativity a pure three-contact receipt); normed fusion stops at the octonions; the self-dual worlds are the unitary orbit |GU(N/2,2)| (3, 18, 648 through six cells); and six cells are the first hidden world, a hexacode phase invisible to every pairwise and triple probe. The native global object is an evolving bridge code. A forcing audit then proves those closure laws are not selected by the floor over matched lawful alternatives (a doubly-even self-dual [24,12,4] counterworld to Golay; the scale-free bridge determinant; two valid triality alphabets; a dual pole rather than self-duality; E_8+E_8+E_8's 720 roots), and a dynamic selection-equivalence theorem shows dynamics only relocates a conserved selector, so the floor forces the atlas of lawful closures and the terminal self-dual class but never the specific member; selection of a world-phase is a conserved received input. Given an actual phase, counting forces the FORM of its response (a one-parameter positive equivariant weight family whose equal-ticket point is the 24-cell Born kernel, with a real amplitude calculus from the retained Z_2 sign scar) and its binding arity, but the Born magnitude law (equal tickets) and the complex phase are received, not forced. Named objects are recovered in a derivational role; the result is structural under named closure axioms, with no metric, spectrum, dimensionful constant, or nature-realization claimed. Three dependency-free scripts verify the chapter from a clean clone in exact arithmetic."
version: "0.9.0"
